Theorem IA-1: Intraprocedural analysis rule signatures — IA-1 through IA-9

  Preconditions:
    - Intraprocedural analysis is the per-function backward dataflow producing
      a converged AimsStateMap per Annex E §AIMS
    - Step 4 of the AIMS pipeline (analyze_function) runs this analysis
      per Annex E §AIMS §6
    - Convergence depends on monotone transfer (L-6) + finite chain height
      per Annex E §AIMS IA-7
    - 9 IA rules govern direction / ordering / merging / widening / convergence /
      immortal exclusion per Annex E §AIMS

  Soundness property:
    IA-1 (backward-direction soundness):
      type : Function -> AimsStateMap
      block-entry state is computed from block-exit by walking instructions
      in reverse; bidirectional interaction with forward TF on per-instruction
      basis (forward sets definition-time dims; backward accumulates use-time
      dims).

    IA-2 (reverse postorder traversal):
      type : Function -> List BlockIndex
      blocks SHALL be processed in reverse postorder; deterministic ordering
      independent of hash-map iteration order.

    IA-3 (block exit state = alt_join over successor entries):
      type : BlockIndex x AimsStateMap -> Map ArcVarId AimsState
      block_exit_state(B) = alt_join over successor_blocks(B).block_entry_states;
      terminal blocks (Return / Resume / Unreachable) seeded from TF-11a
      terminator demands.

    IA-4 (cross-block locality widening):
      type : AimsStateMap -> AimsStateMap
      variables flowing across block boundaries SHALL have
      locality := max(locality, fl) (FunctionLocal).

    IA-5 (per-instruction transfer — two-step):
      type : AimsState x ArcInstr -> AimsState
      step (1): backward-transfer-of-forward — transparent alias / borrow /
                Select / aggregate-builder / non-alias cases handled per
                Annex E §AIMS IA-5 instruction-type matrix
      step (2): backward-demand-accumulation per TF-11 — operands receive
                additive demand via seq_add

    IA-6 (return-value widening):
      type : AimsStateMap -> AimsStateMap
      return values widened to (access := O, locality := max(locality, he));
      applies at Return-instruction points only.

    IA-7 (convergence bound):
      type : Function -> Int
      iteration limit = CHAIN_HEIGHT x |variables| x |blocks|,
        CHAIN_HEIGHT = 16 (sum of dim heights: 1+3+2+2+4+1+3);
      on exceeded -> widen all to TOP (O, U, omega, s, top, Phi, ALL)
      (NOTE: uses s for Uniqueness, NOT ms — safety net).

    IA-8 (immortal-variable exclusion):
      type : Function -> Set ArcVarId
      immortal vars (heap-allocated constants with MAX_REFCOUNT detected
      by aims/immortal/ pre-pass) excluded from worklist; treated as scalars.

    IA-9 (N-ary join permutation invariance):
      type : List AimsState -> AimsState
      fold order over successor states SHALL NOT affect result;
      follows from L-1 (commutativity) + L-2 (associativity) of join.

    Closes opencode S01-R0-F3 IA-category-omission finding: §06 dispatch
    consumes these 9 signatures + sec-06 discharges per-rule theorems
    (IA-1 through IA-9 in the 124-rule inventory).

